MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Assuming Goin' Home is Kenny Wayne Shepherd's album, its guitar blues feels like a natural next listen after my Hendrix and Clapton albums.",
    "The Rolling Stones' blues roots and, if it is by Tedeschi Trucks Band, Revelator's blues sound connect with what I want now; the Eagles also fit part of my classic-rock taste."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Mamas & the Papas' harmony-driven pop, Earth Wind & Fire's funk and soul, and ELO's orchestral pop rock do not satisfy my current interest in bluesy guitar.",
    "Even when I like the artist, a greatest-hits collection is less appealing today than exploring an album; titles such as Very Best Of give me too little evidence of a musical match."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in some classic-rock artists seems to have been stretched into an interest in older popular music generally.",
    "The repeated greatest-hits selections assume I want familiar songs, although my recent choices give more reason to suggest albums to explore."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The blues guitar connection in my Hendrix and Clapton listening matters more to me right now than a broad classic-rock connection.",
    "I rarely choose something without a clear musical reason, so an uncertain artist identity leaves me hesitant even when an album title sounds promising."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You partly recognized my classic-rock interests, but missed how strongly blues guitar and album exploration guide my choices right now."
}
